---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Maintainer guide"
  description="A practical workflow for maintaining the Technion Fractals Seminar website."
>
  <header class="page-header maintainer-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Website operations</p>
    <h1>Maintainer guide</h1>
    <p>A practical workflow for reviewing submissions, publishing talks, and keeping the website reliable.</p>
    <div class="guide-actions">
      <a class="button" href="https://app.pagescms.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Open Pages CMS ↗
      </a>
      <a
        class="secondary-action"
        href="https://github.com/technionfractals/technionfractals.github.io/actions"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        View deployments ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="guide-content">
    <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-number">01</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="workflow-heading">From submission to publication</h2>
          <p>The normal path requires no local code changes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ol class="workflow">
        <li>
          <strong>Collect</strong>
          <span>Review the speaker's Google Form response.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Confirm</strong>
          <span>Resolve missing dates, venue details, links, or unclear wording.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Draft</strong>
          <span>Create the talk in Pages CMS and keep its status as draft.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Review</strong>
          <span>Check the rendered abstract, mathematical notation, and public materials.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Publish</strong>
          <span>Set the status to published and save the CMS entry.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Verify</strong>
          <span>Wait for GitHub Actions, then inspect the public page.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="talk-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-number">02</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="talk-heading">Add or edit a talk</h2>
          <p>In Pages CMS, choose <strong>Talks</strong>, then create a new entry or open an existing one.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Title and speaker</h3>
          <p>Use the final public title. Confirm the speaker's name, affiliation, and optional homepage.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Schedule and venue</h3>
          <p>Use local Technion time. Enter the venue in the compact format <code>RM 864, Amado</code>.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Tags</h3>
          <p>Add concise search keywords as separate list items. Tags help visitors find a talk but are not displayed on the website.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Abstract</h3>
          <p>Proofread the Markdown. Inline math uses <code>$...$</code>. For display math, use Source mode and place the opening and closing <code>$$</code> on separate lines:</p>
          <pre class="math-example"><code>{`$$
e^{i\\pi} + 1 = 0
$$`}</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Materials</h3>
          <p>Add verified public links or files only. Use short labels such as Note, Slides, Poster, or Reference.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <aside class="callout">
        <strong>Publication status</strong>
        <p>Keep incomplete entries as <code>draft</code>. Only entries marked <code>published</code> should appear publicly.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="schema-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-number">03</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="schema-heading">Content schema reference</h2>
          <p>Use these shapes when editing files directly. Pages CMS creates the same structure for you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="schema-reference">
        <h3>Complete talk example</h3>
        <pre><code>{`---
title: 'When does $\dim_H(E)=s$?'              # Required; inline LaTeX is allowed
speaker: "Ada Example"                       # Required
affiliation: "Technion"                      # Optional
date: 2026-10-08                             # Required: YYYY-MM-DD
startTime: "14:30"                           # Required: 24-hour HH:mm
endTime: "15:30"                             # Required: 24-hour HH:mm
venue: "RM 864, Amado"                       # Required
status: published                            # draft, published, or cancelled
speakerUrl: "https://example.com/"            # Optional homepage
tags:                                        # Optional hidden search keywords
  - self-similar-measures
  - dimension-theory
  - entropy
summary: "Optional short plain-text abstract." # Optional; replaces the body below
resources:                                   # Optional; any number and order
  - type: link                               # Visible link row
    label: "Video"
    url: "https://example.com/video"
  - type: note                               # Collapsible Markdown and LaTeX
    label: "Note"
    text: |-
      A short note with inline math $s > 0$.
  - type: text                               # Visible text without a label
    text: "Slides will be added after the talk."
---

Write the full Markdown abstract here. It is used when summary is omitted.`}</code></pre>

        <p class="schema-note"><strong>Resources:</strong> <code>link</code> requires <code>label</code> and <code>url</code>; <code>note</code> requires <code>label</code> and <code>text</code>; unlabeled <code>text</code> requires only <code>text</code>.</p>

        <h3>Participant example</h3>
        <pre><code>{`{
  "name": "Ada Example",                 // Required
  "url": "https://example.com/",         // Optional homepage
  "email": "ada@example.com",            // Optional
  "showEmail": true                       // Optional; defaults to false
}`}</code></pre>
        <p class="schema-note">An email is displayed only when <code>email</code> is present and <code>showEmail</code> is <code>true</code>.</p>

        <h3>Contact item example</h3>
        <pre><code>{`{
  "label": "Email",
  "value": "technionfractals AT gmail.com"
}`}</code></pre>
        <p class="schema-note">Contact is a repeatable list. Add, remove, or reorder labeled items in Pages CMS.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="check-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-number">04</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="check-heading">Pre-publication check</h2>
          <p>A short final review prevents most public corrections.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Speaker name and affiliation are spelled correctly.</li>
        <li>Date, weekday, start time, end time, and venue agree.</li>
        <li>Abstract paragraphs and mathematical notation render correctly.</li>
        <li>Speaker homepage and material links open successfully.</li>
        <li>No private files or personal contact details are exposed.</li>
        <li>The talk appears on the intended Upcoming or Previous page.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="settings-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-number">05</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="settings-heading">Update seminar information</h2>
          <p>Use <strong>Seminar settings</strong> in Pages CMS for information shared across the website.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="compact-list">
        <p><strong>General:</strong> the title shown in the header, browser title, and footer.</p>
        <p><strong>Upcoming:</strong> the description shown below the Upcoming talks heading.</p>
        <p><strong>Submit:</strong> the public Google Form URL used by the Submit page.</p>
        <p><strong>About:</strong> the page description, participants, and repeatable Contact list.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="technical-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-number">06</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="technical-heading">Technical changes</h2>
          <p>Use the local repository for layout, code, dependencies, and CMS configuration.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="code-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>Prepare and preview</h3>
          <pre><code>git pull --ff-only
pnpm install
pnpm dev</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Validate and publish</h3>
          <pre><code>pnpm build
git add --all
git commit -m "describe the change"
git push origin main</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="recovery-heading">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-number">07</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="recovery-heading">Deployment and recovery</h2>
          <p>Every Pages CMS save and every push to <code>main</code> starts the GitHub Pages workflow.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="recovery-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>If content is wrong</h3>
          <p>Correct the entry in Pages CMS and save again. The corrective commit will trigger a fresh deployment.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>If deployment fails</h3>
          <p>Open the failed GitHub Actions run, inspect the first error, and reproduce it locally with <code>pnpm build</code>.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="prototype-note">
      <p class="note-label">Demonstration content</p>
      <p>
        The repository currently contains 66 fictional talk records for testing search, pagination, and the CMS.
        Each record can now be edited or replaced through Pages CMS. Replace the fictional content before public launch.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .maintainer-header {
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .maintainer-header .eyebrow,
  .note-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.55rem;
    color: var(--logistics-blue);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .maintainer-header > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    max-width: 45rem;
  }

  .guide-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .guide-actions .button {
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
  }

  .secondary-action {
    color: var(--blue-hover);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .secondary-action:hover {
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  .guide-content {
    margin-inline: clamp(0.5rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
  }

  .guide-section {
    padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .section-number {
    margin: 0.12rem 0 0;
    color: var(--logistics-blue);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .section-heading h2,
  .field-grid h3,
  .schema-reference h3,
  .code-grid h3,
  .recovery-grid h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section-heading h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .section-heading p:not(.section-number) {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0.55rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .workflow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: workflow;
  }

  .workflow li {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 2.7rem 1rem 0 0;
    counter-increment: workflow;
  }

  .workflow li::before {
    content: counter(workflow, decimal-leading-zero);
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    display: grid;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: white;
    background: var(--logistics-blue);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .workflow li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.95rem;
    left: 2.25rem;
    width: calc(100% - 2.6rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .workflow strong,
  .workflow span {
    display: block;
  }

  .workflow strong {
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  .workflow span {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .field-grid,
  .code-grid,
  .recovery-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-left: 3.3rem;
  }

  .field-grid article,
  .recovery-grid article {
    padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .field-grid h3,
  .schema-reference h3,
  .code-grid h3,
  .recovery-grid h3 {
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .field-grid p,
  .recovery-grid p {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.91rem;
  }

  .field-grid .math-example {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
  }

  .schema-reference {
    margin-left: 3.3rem;
  }

  .schema-reference h3:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .schema-note {
    max-width: 58rem;
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.91rem;
  }

  code {
    padding: 0.08rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 0.2rem;
    color: var(--blue);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--logistics-blue) 8%, var(--paper));
    font-size: 0.88em;
  }

  .callout,
  .prototype-note {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--logistics-blue);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--logistics-blue) 6%, var(--paper));
  }

  .callout {
    margin: 1rem 0 0 3.3rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
  }

  .callout p {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .checklist {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.7rem 2rem;
    margin: 0 0 0 3.3rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .checklist li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }

  .checklist li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.58em;
    left: 0;
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    background: var(--logistics-blue);
  }

  .compact-list {
    margin-left: 3.3rem;
  }

  .compact-list p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .compact-list p + p {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
  }

  .code-grid > div {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  pre {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--logistics-blue) 5%, var(--paper));
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  pre code {
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
    background: none;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .prototype-note {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
  }

  .prototype-note p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prototype-note p:last-child {
    max-width: 60rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 58rem) {
    .workflow {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem 0;
    }

    .workflow li:nth-child(3)::after {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 42rem) {
    .workflow,
    .field-grid,
    .code-grid,
    .recovery-grid,
    .checklist {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .workflow {
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .workflow li {
      min-height: 2rem;
      padding: 0 0 0 3rem;
    }

    .workflow li::after {
      display: none;
    }

    .field-grid,
    .code-grid,
    .recovery-grid,
    .checklist,
    .compact-list,
    .schema-reference {
      margin-left: 0;
    }

    .callout {
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
